# shir_nodes/char_translate.node — expression-level semantic IR node.
# Translate/delete/squeeze characters (lowered from `tr SET1 SET2`).
#
# Backends: Perl tr///, JS regex/lookup, C ctype, Rust chars().map()
# Fallback: sh2.translate(text, from, to, delete, squeeze)
#
# ShIR_TextOps_Strings proves `char_translate_sound`, one law per mode: translation
# preserves length and, with equal-length sets, IS the per-byte map `map_of` over
# `zip from to`; `tr`'s short-target rule (the last member of SET2 repeats) is visible
# in `tr_expand`; delete mode removes exactly the SET1 bytes (`set s - set from`); and
# squeeze collapses runs of SET2 to one byte, invents nothing and shrinks the text
# (`no_run`, subset, length bound). OUT OF MODEL: `tr`'s range syntax `a-z`, character
# classes, escapes and `-c` — `from`/`to` are already-expanded byte strings, and range
# expansion is the lowering's job, not the node's.

node CharTranslate
tag "CharTranslate"
kind expr
# storage_class str_bounded
field text: expr
field from: string
field to: string
field delete: bool
field squeeze: bool
spec: TextOps#char_translate_sound
